Money in this biography does not accumulate; it **arrives in lumps and

exits through standing drains.** This page traces the capital timeline as

a single causal chain — from the two family source-lines, through the

2020 estate distribution, the market era, the wage years, and the

decade's largest single drain, down to the 2026 state (broke, housed on

an unpapered arrangement with a lien clock running). Read as one system,

the spine explains the biography's central financial puzzle: how a life

positioned downstream of genuine family capital — a coal-region estate

on one side, a successful auto-parts chain on the other — repeatedly

lands at water-shutoff poverty, and why every capital arrival dissipates

on a timescale of months.

