## The largest drain

The decade's biggest documented capital flow is not rent, drugs, or the

market. It is [[wiki/people/annie-ulmer|Annie]]: ~$139K sent against

~$16–20K received across Cash App and Venmo — a net outflow of roughly

**$119K–$123K**, approximately the size of the entire estate

distribution. The financial history of the relationship is a

three-rotation see-saw (Dan funds the early NYC years → Dan works

through the 2023 landlord-debt stretch → Annie sole earner through 2024

after the involuntary job loss), but the see-saw's net is six-to-one in

her favor. Set against the source-lines, the spine's shape is complete:

**family capital entered from two lines Dan never controlled, and the

largest share of what reached him exited through a relationship whose

terminal phase ran on him controlling her supply** — the money and the

supply network are the same architecture at different layers.

